  "interpretation": [
    "All six runs reported security_passed=true, unique ingress IDs, 204 protected records/run and zero owned contexts/maskers after shutdown.",
    "All six runs reported functional_passed=false due to fail-closed outcomes and caller deadlines.",
    "Platform 10 callers: 176/200 normally masked vs virtual 82/200. At 50: 69 vs 22. At 100: 31 vs 29. Do not infer causal thread-mode benefit from one sequentially ordered A/B trial.",
    "At 100 callers both modes saturated the 64-request bounded queue: 70 overload rejections each. Higher all-log-call throughput largely reflects fail-closed records, not actual normal masking throughput.",
    "Physical write-order inversions are expected; numerically sorted per-instance ingress sequences recovered all protected records, but fail-closed output discards original eventId so exact original-to-failure attribution cannot be independently proved from the protected file alone.",
    "Post-stop working set returned to roughly 167-170 MiB in all six samples; these are endpoint memory snapshots, not an in-flight peak or soak/leak test.",
    "No repeated randomized A/B trials were run, and run order was platform first then virtual; system workload and operating environment were not held constant."
